  "_comment": "Physical baseline for the dry-compound fit (fit.py). Offsets are seconds vs the softest compound; wear is seconds per lap of tyre age. The fit enforces the ordering (softer = faster and wears faster) and shrinks each adjacent-compound step toward the difference of these priors with the weight of `pseudoLaps` laps of evidence. Wet compounds are unordered and unshrunk. freshTyre: a bonus (s, negative = faster) on the first clean laps of a new set, at full weight on the first and fading linearly over `laps` laps; its prior is the lap-weighted pooled estimate from the tuning races only (-0.21s), shrunk with `pseudoLaps`. Eras (eras build plan 1.2): a block for each schema era; _copiedFrom marks a block copied from that era's until it's tuned.",
